## Context

Memo `conception/2026-10-31-monitoring-redesign.md` § 4.4. The author wants timeline bars of the execution flow
(session, subagents, seats, tool calls, test and gate runs) with timings and
costs, and pointers back into the transcripts. Part of tracker 1382.

Two scripts:

- `scripts/trace_events.py`: a module, one reader per runtime (Claude Code
  with `subagents/`, Codex rollouts with cumulative `token_count` turned into
  differences, Pi sessions) yielding events with the same fields: kind, name,
  start, end, model, tokens, shadow USD, exit, pointer `(file, call id)`, the
  call id being each runtime's own (`tool_use_id`, Codex `call_id`, Pi
  `toolCallId`; aider: file only). Shadow USD from the price table now in
  `scripts/trace-stats.py:34`, moved into this module and imported back;
  OpenAI rows added with source and date; an unpriced model shows
  `cost unknown`, never zero.
  It is the reader a later index will reuse (memo § 5), so it holds no
  rendering code.
- `scripts/trace_timeline.py <session>`: reads the session, its subagents and
  the seats its launch lines (1384) name, live tree first then archive (1383),
  and writes Chrome Trace Event JSON: one lane per concurrent agent, one
  complete event per tool call, pointer and costs in `args`. Background
  commands end at their completion notification.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Fixture test per runtime reader (Claude Code, Codex, Pi): events with
      start, end, tokens and pointer; Codex per-turn tokens are differences
- [ ] Fixture test: a Codex event of a priced model carries shadow USD; an
      unpriced model's event says `cost unknown`
- [ ] Fixture test: overlapping subagents land on distinct lanes; a seat named
      by a launch line lands under its parent
- [ ] One raid session of the week renders in Perfetto with at least one
      non-Claude seat; three events
      spot-checked against the transcript lines their pointers name (quoted in
      the PR)
- [ ] `trace_timeline.py` reads a session already pruned from the live tree from
      the archive

## Raid 8ad75a plan annotation (2026-10-31, lead)

Phases 2-3 compressed (see 1380). Feasibility: WARN. Plan text: /tmp/raid-8ad75a/plan-1385.md (host padme). Wave 2, after 1383 and 1384 merge.

Path: stdlib `scripts/trace_events.py` (frozen Event dataclass; read_claude / read_codex / read_pi / read_aider; PRICING + price; open_transcript live-first then archive via `zstd -dc`) and `scripts/trace_timeline.py` (greedy interval lanes, Chrome Trace JSON written directly, no Perfetto library).
Lead rulings:
- PRICING is at `trace-stats.py:36`; trace-stats re-exports `PRICING` and `resolve_pricing` (spec-loaded by four scripts). OpenAI rows must not break `trace-hypotheses.py:70,138` (`cache_write_5m` key, `_MAX_PRICING`): same keys or a separate table; run `tests/test_trace_*`.
- OpenAI prices looked up from the official pricing page, URL and date in a comment, only models seen in local rollouts; unknown -> `cost unknown` (None), never 0.
- Pi cost taken as recorded, labelled `pi-recorded` (a recorded 0 for a local model shows as such, not as table-priced).
- Archive path and host via `transcript_spool` (1383); launches via `launch_line`'s path (1384).
- Fixtures hand-written, no real transcript content.
